%% MyStreet.id — Editor & Save Workflow (Spec Section 4: Workflow Editor dan Penyimpanan)
%% Local-first: "saving" writes to the Local Draft Cache in the browser. There is
%% no server round-trip. The repository validates data before trusting it.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User
    participant Editor as Editor UI
    participant Preview as Live Preview
    participant Repo as PortfolioRepository
    participant Cache as Local Draft Cache (browser)

    User->>Editor: Edit a field
    Editor->>Preview: Update preview (debounced, local)
    Editor->>Repo: save(draft)
    Repo->>Repo: Validate with zod schema
    alt Valid
        Repo->>Cache: Write draft (localStorage / IndexedDB)
        Cache-->>Repo: Ack (local, synchronous-ish)
        Repo-->>Editor: SaveState = saved
        Editor-->>User: Show "Saved locally"
    else Invalid
        Repo-->>Editor: ValidationErrors
        Editor-->>User: Show inline errors (no data lost)
    end

    Note over Repo,Cache: No network, no server. Data never leaves this browser\nunless the user explicitly exports it.
